From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a shader effect draws meshes, images and arrays

A shell's shader effect can now draw the content through a mesh, sample
images, and read array uniforms the shell sets per element.

- cc::FilterOperation's SHADER filter gains its arrays, at most 16384
  floats (64 KiB), which cross mojo, and opaque inputs that viz attaches
  with the program and that never cross it. An animation keeps the arrays
  the page committed: EffectTree::OnFilterAnimated takes them from the
  node's filters.
- The privileged DomicileShaderEffects.Register takes a source: the
  fragment program, a vertex program over a grid or instances, and up to
  four RGBA images. It answers with the array uniforms the effect takes.
- SurfaceAggregator mipmaps a pass whose quad has a mesh effect, so the
  pass is drawn to a texture and never bypassed. SkiaRenderer draws that
  quad with drawMesh, on a layer that takes the other filters, the mask,
  the opacity and the blend mode.
- Blink attaches an element's arrays when it builds its filters, and
  composites a filter animation whose only pixel-moving filters are
  shader effects with the same outsets in every keyframe.
- Two dictionaries, DomicileShaderEffectInit and DomicileShaderEffectImage,
  are registered with the bindings.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine job builds it on `crux`.
